course: dictionary
lesson: 10578
title: Plain and undecorated
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Undecorated is a long word, but you can break it into parts. Un- means not, decorate means to add things to make something look nice, and -ed shows it describes something. So undecorated means not decorated, with nothing added to make it pretty.
explain: Look at the clues around it. «He had got down to the bare bones of it, and they were fine and strong and simple.» The next part says he liked the countryside «undecorated, hard, and stripped of its finery». Bare, simple and stripped all point to plain, so undecorated fits.
explain: The word can also describe a soldier. A soldier who was never given a medal is undecorated. Before you choose a meaning, ask what the sentence is about: a plain pot or room, or a soldier with no medals?
fact: Undecorated means plain, with no decorations or ornaments.
fact: An undecorated pot or cake is the plain version, before you add patterns or icing.
fact: A soldier who has not been given any medals can be called undecorated.
fact: The prefix un- means not, so undecorated means not decorated.
fact: «Stripped» means taken away, so «stripped of its finery» means the fancy extras were removed.
exercise: «The cake was undecorated, so Ava added icing and sprinkles.» What does undecorated mean? | Burnt and black | Covered in sweets | Iced and finished | *Plain, with no icing or sprinkles yet
exercise: Sam's grandad was a soldier who was never given a medal. Which word describes him? | *Undecorated | Luminous | Ancient | Curt
exercise: Mrs Hale says, «Bring me an undecorated pot so you can paint your own patterns.» What does she want? | A pot with a broken handle | *A plain pot with no patterns on it yet | A pot with lots of painted flowers | A pot that is already finished and shiny
test: «The bare walls of the room were undecorated.» What does undecorated mean here? | *Plain, with no pictures or ornaments | Painted in bright colours | Very cold and dark | Covered in medals
test: Why would an art teacher ask pupils to start with an undecorated pot? | To paint their own patterns on it later | *To keep it hidden in a cupboard | Because it is already finished | Because it has medals on it
exam: Mia's grandad says he was an undecorated soldier. What does this mean? | He won every medal in the war | He had decorated his uniform with stars | *He was never given a medal | He was a famous hero with a statue in the park
